WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.832
EDR telemetry is the activity data collected from endpoints.

2
00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:19.496
Common examples include process starts, command-line arguments, file writes, network connections, user logins, privilege changes, script activity, service creation, scheduled tasks, and registry modifications.

3
00:00:19.496 --> 00:00:22.340
A single event may not mean much by itself.

4
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.326
The value comes from context.

5
00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:30.223
A command-line tool might be normal for an administrator but suspicious on a receptionist's laptop.

6
00:00:30.223 --> 00:00:35.232
A network connection may be normal for one application but strange for another.

7
00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:43.344
EDR helps analysts connect events into a timeline so they can understand whether activity is benign, suspicious, or malicious.

8
00:00:43.344 --> 00:00:53.311
That timeline can show what started first, what process launched another process, which user was involved, what network destination was contacted, and what files changed.
